<div class="sec-hdr">Section 4 - CUSTOMER OBLIGATIONS</div>
<p><span class="bold ital">IMPORTANT: in order to keep Your Contract valid, the following MUST be adhered to:</span></p>
<p>At maximum intervals of 12,000 km from the purchase or lease date, you must, at your own expense:</p>
<ul>
  <li><span class="bold">have the engine oil and filter changed</span></li>
  <li><span class="bold">have all other fluid levels checked</span><br/>
    <span style="font-size:7.5pt;">(Maintaining proper fluid levels at all times will help make your vehicle safer and more reliable, and will protect it against avoidable breakdowns.)</span>
  </li>
</ul>
<p class="bold">Within 15 calendar days of having the required maintenance performed on your vehicle, please report it to AProtect in ONE of the following ways:</p>
<ul>
  <li><span class="bold">WEBSITE:</span> complete online form located at oilchange.aprotect.com</li>
  <li><span class="bold">EMAIL</span> a copy of the invoice with your Contract number clearly indicated, to: info@a-protectwarranty.com</li>
  <li><span class="bold">MAIL</span> a copy of the invoice, with your Contract number clearly indicated, to: AProtect Warranty Corporation, 8800 Dufferin St. Suite 302B, Concord, Ontario L4K 0C5</li>
</ul>
<p>In all cases, please ensure that you keep the original invoices. Should You make a claim under the Contract, You may be required to provide these original invoices.</p>
<p class="bold">Do-it-Yourself oil changes are NOT ACCEPTABLE.</p>
<p class="bold">Failure to comply with all of the above constitutes non-performance of the conditions and may operate to void this Contract. A grace period of 1,000 km will be allowed with regards to the maintenance requirements described above.</p>
<p><span class="bold">A.</span> Repairs made to covered components without prior authorization by Lubrico Warranty (1-800-265-1510) will not be reimbursed. Please refer to the Terms and Conditions for complete details.</p>
<p><span class="bold">B.</span> In signing the Application for the Lubrico Vehicle Service Contract, the Contract Holder has certified that they:</p>
<ol>
  <li>have read, accepted and understand the Terms and Conditions of the Contract as set forth in this document,</li>
  <li>acknowledged that the Selling Dealer has made no representations outside of the Terms and Conditions,</li>
  <li>understand that Application for coverage must be made at time of vehicle purchase or prior to the expiration of an existing manufacturer's warranty,</li>
  <li>understand that changes cannot be made to the Contract regarding coverage and options chosen after acceptance by Lubrico,</li>
  <li>confirm that the information herein is true, accurate and the vehicle was in proper operating condition at the date of purchase (i.e. date of Application for Lubrico Vehicle Service Contract).</li>
</ol>
<p class="bold">Please Note: Misleading information will void this Contract.</p>
<p>In signing the Application for the Lubrico Vehicle Service Contract, the Selling Dealer has certified that the registered vehicle qualifies for the coverage option chosen above, the information provided is correct, the vehicle is in proper operating condition, that no representations have been made outside of the Terms and Conditions and that the Contract Holder has been given a copy of the Contract Application at the time of sale.</p>

